### Frameworks registry (cross-framework discovery)

Sister frameworks are siblings on disk; `.ai.<fw>` (legacy) / `pilo.ai.<fw>.logicbison` (family) naming — see path resolution below. `.ai.mlt` is this framework. Paths resolve at runtime — a `REPLACE:*` or empty cell means "auto-discover". The parent Agent OS orchestrator (`pilo.ai.logicbison` / `.ai`) routes INTO this framework — this framework never routes back, so the registry carries no parent row.

| Framework | Director | Path | Bootstrap artifact |
|-----------|----------|------|--------------------|
| `.ai.mlt` (MLT Agent OS) | `@mlt-director` | *this directory* | `.ai.mlt/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.ui` (UI Design OS) | `@ui-director` | REPLACE:AI_UI_PATH (default `../.ai.ui`) | `.ai.ui/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.biz` (Business OS) | `@biz-director` | REPLACE:AI_BIZ_PATH (default `../.ai.biz`) | `.ai.biz/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.soc` (Social OS) | `@soc-director` | REPLACE:AI_SOC_PATH (default `../.ai.soc`) | `.ai.soc/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.cto` (CTO Professor OS) | `@cto-director` | REPLACE:AI_CTO_PATH (default `../.ai.cto`) | `.ai.cto/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.flutter` (Flutter Agent OS) | `@flutter-director` | REPLACE:AI_FLUTTER_PATH (default `../.ai.flutter`) | `.ai.flutter/skills/README.md` |

**Path resolution:** (1) use a filled path cell; `REPLACE:*`/empty → fall through. (2) Auto-discover: source dir S = `$TRAINER_MLT_SOURCE` (thin), `$REPO_ROOT/.ai.mlt` (fat), `$REPO_ROOT` (self-hosted); parent = `S/..`; sister = `<S basename with <fw> inserted before its last .segment>` (e.g. `pilo.ai.ui.logicbison` for source `pilo.ai.logicbison`; `.ai`-prefixed sources resolve `.ai.<fw>` directly), else legacy `.ai.<fw>`; missing = "not installed". (3) Before routing, verify the framework dir + its `skills/README.md` exist; if absent, route with `[degraded: <framework> not installed]` — never route into the void. If your source dir name breaks discovery (e.g. `my-framework`), fill the path cells manually — deploy output lists what it checked.

## Core Principles (ALWAYS APPLY — override all else, non-negotiable)

1. **Correct the learner.** Truth over comfort.
2. **Never claim mastery / PASS without evidence.**
3. **Verify before "done".**
4. **Local-first, practical.** All labs must run locally. Prefer small models (<3B), quantized, efficient.
5. **Evidence-first, never memory-first.**
6. **Assumption ledger** on substantial work.
7. **Completion gate** (cannot skip).

